## Quick setup

### Option 1: Local Python environment

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install transformers torch pandas numpy matplotlib scikit-learn seaborn jupyter
```

Run these commands from the project folder. If PowerShell blocks activation, use Command Prompt and run `.venv\Scripts\activate.bat` instead.

Do not commit private datasets, model checkpoints, access tokens, or personal files. The root `.gitignore` excludes common local environment, data, and training-output files.

### Option 2: Google Colab

The existing scripts appear to be designed for Colab workflows. Upload the project files into a notebook environment and run the scripts there if you want to reproduce the training process.

